INT. BANK – DAY

A quiet weekday afternoon.

Customers wait in line. CASHIERS work behind the glass. A SECURITY GUARD watches the entrance.

The doors open.

A MAN IN A SANTA COSTUME walks in, carrying a large red GIFT BAG.

He stops.

Looks around.

A few customers smile.

CUSTOMER
Merry Christmas!

Santa doesn't respond.

He slowly places the gift bag on the floor.

The smile disappears from his face.

SANTA
Nobody move.

The room freezes.

The SECURITY GUARD reaches instinctively toward his radio.

Santa notices.

SANTA
Don't.

The guard stops.

Santa steps toward the counter.

SANTA
Fill the bag.

The HEAD CASHIER stares at him.

HEAD CASHIER
What...?

Santa leans closer.

SANTA
Money.

A frightened customer begins crying.

Santa turns toward the room.

SANTA
I'm not here to hurt anybody.

A beat.

SANTA (CONT'D)
But if I don't walk out of here with that bag full... somebody gets hurt.

The Head Cashier looks at the other employees.

Slowly, they begin putting cash into the bag.

Santa watches.

His hands tremble slightly.

He's trying very hard to look in control.

A LITTLE GIRL, holding her mother's hand, stares at him.

LITTLE GIRL
Are you really Santa?

Santa looks at her.

For a moment, the threat in his eyes disappears.

He looks almost heartbroken.

SANTA
Not today.

The bag is finally pushed toward him.

Santa grabs it.

The alarm suddenly BLARES.

Everyone flinches.

Santa freezes.

He looks toward the exit.

Then back at the frightened people.

A long beat.

He picks up the bag.

SANTA
I'm sorry.

He runs.

The doors swing open behind him.

The bank remains frozen in silence.

Then—

SECURITY GUARD
Call the police!

CUT TO BLACK.
